4586
04:42:44,500 --> 04:42:48,060
I think the only real spoiler we've ever gotten was related to Totem of Undying.

4587
04:42:49,260 --> 04:42:50,360
Yeah, I remember that.

4588
04:42:51,700 --> 04:42:53,340
I actually kind of forgot about that item.

4589
04:42:55,180 --> 04:42:56,180
But yeah, that's the thing.

4590
04:42:57,240 --> 04:42:58,940
If you hold it in your hand, you won't die.

4591
04:42:59,540 --> 04:43:04,220
I don't think I would have ever figured that one out if it wasn't for that spoiler.

4592
04:43:05,340 --> 04:43:06,280
Because let's be real.

4593
04:43:06,940 --> 04:43:08,220
How would you ever know?

4594
04:43:08,900 --> 04:43:11,700
I would never try to hold that in my hand when I have a shield, right?

4595
04:43:15,630 --> 04:43:18,610
You were also spoiled with the elytra and rockets when you went on the server.

4596
04:43:18,730 --> 04:43:21,350
Yeah, I don't think I would have figured out the rockets, guys.

4597
04:43:22,250 --> 04:43:23,970
The elytra would still have been great, though.

4598
04:43:25,350 --> 04:43:26,770
Because I can still float with it, right?

4599
04:43:29,610 --> 04:43:30,830
It's annoying to hold it all the time.

4600
04:43:30,930 --> 04:43:37,770
Yeah, it would have to be something where you have it on a keybind, and if you know you're about to die, you hit that keybind so you have it, right?

4601
04:43:49,830 --> 04:43:51,870
I was spoiled on how to use nametags, was I?

4602
04:43:51,950 --> 04:43:52,510
I don't remember.

4603
04:43:55,370 --> 04:43:57,010
I don't remember that at all, was I?

4604
04:43:57,790 --> 04:43:58,890
Was that in season one?

4605
04:44:03,530 --> 04:44:06,670
You were lucky to avoid some big spoilers in the April Fool's snapshot.

4606
04:44:06,830 --> 04:44:07,890
Oh, that's good.

4607
04:44:09,510 --> 04:44:11,270
I guess nobody would know, right?

4608
04:44:11,350 --> 04:44:12,790
Because we all started on the same level.

4609
04:44:13,210 --> 04:44:14,470
Nobody really knew what was in there.

4610
04:44:21,850 --> 04:44:24,210
It was in the map we made for you in the museum at the end.

4611
04:44:24,350 --> 04:44:25,430
Ah, I see!

4612
04:44:26,150 --> 04:44:27,050
That explains it.

4613
04:44:29,150 --> 04:44:29,510
Yeah.

4614
04:44:33,190 --> 04:44:35,610
People were saying that the MC movie doesn't have spoilers.

4615
04:44:36,330 --> 04:44:37,810
You know what people also have been saying?

4616
04:44:38,270 --> 04:44:39,390
That it's not a good movie.

4617
04:44:40,310 --> 04:44:42,650
But obviously, I mean, you gotta make your own opinion, right?

4618
04:44:44,530 --> 04:44:48,270
But I saw the trailer for it, and... I don't know, man.

4619
04:44:48,830 --> 04:44:49,370
It's rough.

4620
04:44:50,090 --> 04:44:51,510
I think I'll check it out with a friend.

4621
04:44:52,450 --> 04:44:54,730
And just sit there and throw plastic spoons, you know?

4622
04:44:57,270 --> 04:44:57,850
Yeah, exactly.

4623
04:44:57,990 --> 04:44:59,090
As long as it's a fun experience.

4624
04:45:05,580 --> 04:45:08,460
But the thing is, I like Jack Black, so maybe he'll carry it for me.

4625
04:45:08,820 --> 04:45:11,940
I just like... his person, you know?

4626
04:45:12,100 --> 04:45:12,800
I think he's funny.

4627
04:45:13,520 --> 04:45:13,900
Mostly.

4628
04:45:17,750 --> 04:45:21,290
That museum spoiler many things, thankfully you've forgotten 99% of it all.

4629
04:45:21,390 --> 04:45:26,510
Honestly, oopsie, before you just said that, I had completely forgotten about the museum existing at all.

4630
04:45:29,330 --> 04:45:31,610
I hadn't thought about that ever since.

4631
04:45:32,010 --> 04:45:35,430
Maybe a couple times, but not in the last six months, at least.

4632
04:45:38,680 --> 04:45:41,220
And it's not because the museum was forgettable, okay?

4633
04:45:41,400 --> 04:45:46,500
It's just because my brain functions in a way where new stuff comes in, pushes old stuff out.

4634
04:45:46,780 --> 04:45:47,720
It's not optimal.

4635
04:45:48,720 --> 04:45:50,000
The museum was great.

4636
04:45:51,120 --> 04:45:52,100
And pretty.

4637
04:45:53,120 --> 04:45:55,060
Like, the lighting in there was insane.

4638
04:45:55,820 --> 04:45:59,700
Then again, I think I was playing with shaders doing that, so that enhanced it a little bit.

4639
04:46:01,120 --> 04:46:02,880
What else do I remember from the wrap-ups?

4640
04:46:02,940 --> 04:46:03,740
That's a good question.

4641
04:46:04,940 --> 04:46:06,360
I learned about the pyramid.

4642
04:46:07,000 --> 04:46:08,040
How to make the pyramid?

4643
04:46:08,880 --> 04:46:15,200
That one is one of the things I was, I think, close to figuring out in Season 1, but I never did.

4644
04:46:15,620 --> 04:46:18,500
I stopped shortly after that testing phase.

4645
04:46:21,240 --> 04:46:22,320
What is SMP?

4646
04:46:23,420 --> 04:46:24,600
Uh, Ppexi.

4647
04:46:27,730 --> 04:46:29,170
I was 90% of the way.

4648
04:46:29,270 --> 04:46:29,610
Was I?

4649
04:46:31,010 --> 04:46:32,410
I didn't feel like I was.

4650
04:46:33,490 --> 04:46:34,850
Oh, survival multiplayer.

4651
04:46:37,430 --> 04:46:38,590
Oh, okay.

4652
04:46:39,410 --> 04:46:41,790
So you're asking... What did you ask again?

4653
04:46:42,810 --> 04:46:44,510
Have you thought about joining the SMP again?

4654
04:46:45,690 --> 04:46:46,450
Yeah, maybe.

4655
04:46:46,810 --> 04:46:55,250
But I think it would have to be in the very far future again, because I... I don't know, I feel like there's still so many things I want to discover in this game, you know, and...

4656
04:46:55,940 --> 04:46:58,300
I know you guys made some crazy shit on that server.

4657
04:46:59,380 --> 04:47:06,700
So getting on that server, I think it opened my eyes to the possibility, even though it was vague, of what could be done in Minecraft.

4658
04:47:07,420 --> 04:47:12,900
And maybe that fanned a little flame in me thinking, man, something's happening out there, you know, in the distance.

4659
04:47:13,580 --> 04:47:15,340
If you think hard about it enough.

4660
04:47:17,940 --> 04:47:20,860
So I may have these crazy ideas, right, for doing things.

4661
04:47:22,060 --> 04:47:25,660
And somewhere inside of me, I know that it has to be possible somehow.

4662
04:47:26,640 --> 04:47:28,820
There's some way to do it.

4663
04:47:29,440 --> 04:47:30,220
You know what I mean?

4664
04:47:32,440 --> 04:47:35,440
I don't think I'm gonna open the floodgates again, HHF.

4665
04:47:42,040 --> 04:47:46,420
Oliver, you're living proof in the Minecraft community that it's possible to beat the game blind.

4666
04:47:47,280 --> 04:47:49,160
Yeah, but from someone who streamed it, right?

4667
04:47:49,760 --> 04:47:52,240
There's probably many people out there who didn't stream it.

4668
04:47:52,660 --> 04:47:54,040
Most people don't stream games.

4669
04:47:59,280 --> 04:48:03,560
And I also heard of other people doing this before me, so... I'm definitely not the first.

4670
04:48:04,060 --> 04:48:04,820
Streaming it, I mean.

4671
04:48:07,820 --> 04:48:09,340
It is crazy what you can do in Minecraft.

4672
04:48:09,540 --> 04:48:09,900
It is!

4673
04:48:13,940 --> 04:48:17,620
I honestly cannot believe I'm still playing Minecraft in 2025.

4674
04:48:22,880 --> 04:48:24,920
Like... That's changed so much for me, man.

4675
04:48:25,660 --> 04:48:26,720
In terms of gaming.

4676
04:48:27,360 --> 04:48:29,680
Just checking out Minecraft in... was it 2023?

4677
04:48:30,920 --> 04:48:32,380
And it was such a one-off thing.

4678
04:48:32,500 --> 04:48:35,240
I remember on the day, I was just like, pah.

4679
04:48:35,680 --> 04:48:37,060
I'm gonna stream some StarCraft.

4680
04:48:38,080 --> 04:48:39,220
And I was like, ah, you know what?

4681
04:48:39,340 --> 04:48:40,380
Let's try something else.

4682
04:48:40,820 --> 04:48:42,600
And I thought, fuck it, let's try Minecraft.

4683
04:48:42,920 --> 04:48:44,160
You know, the game everyone's playing.

4684
04:48:44,680 --> 04:48:47,000
It was really just a spur-of-the-moment thing.

4685
04:48:50,110 --> 04:48:51,370
Crazy what it has evolved into.

4686
04:48:54,810 --> 04:48:57,410
Did someone make Minecraft in Minecraft with RevStone?

4687
04:48:57,530 --> 04:48:57,890
Shut up.

4688
04:48:58,030 --> 04:48:58,870
That's not real.

4689
04:48:59,190 --> 04:49:00,170
I'm closing you down.

4690
04:49:00,290 --> 04:49:01,290
I'm banning you.

4691
04:49:01,390 --> 04:49:01,730
You're banned.

4692
04:49:03,030 --> 04:49:05,070
For... a couple hours.

4693
04:49:06,310 --> 04:49:08,090
No, I'm out of here, guys.

4694
04:49:08,630 --> 04:49:12,430
Thank you, everyone, for watching today and hanging out and subbing.

4695
04:49:12,530 --> 04:49:13,110
I see you all.

4696
04:49:13,850 --> 04:49:15,670
OneHoop, Vimal, EmRazor.

4697
04:49:16,250 --> 04:49:18,290
Gifted a sub and subscribed as well.

4698
04:49:18,990 --> 04:49:20,290
That's so nice of you, dude.

4699
04:49:21,890 --> 04:49:23,010
It's like getting a hamster.

4700
04:49:23,110 --> 04:49:26,250
You want to get a friend, you know, so they can hang out together in the cage.

4701
04:49:28,710 --> 04:49:31,450
And Onehoop gifted multiple subs I see here.

4702
04:49:31,590 --> 04:49:32,690
You guys are just crazy.

4703
04:49:35,010 --> 04:49:35,730
Evil rat!

4704
04:49:37,690 --> 04:49:38,550
To aimbot.

4705
04:49:39,670 --> 04:49:40,450
Congrats on that one.

4706
04:49:40,970 --> 04:49:41,790
Also, a message here.

4707
04:49:41,910 --> 04:49:43,490
Thanks to Dr. Cray for my sub gift.

4708
04:49:43,570 --> 04:49:44,590
I have the best girlfriend ever.

4709
04:49:45,190 --> 04:49:45,550
Ayyyy.

4710
04:49:46,130 --> 04:49:46,990
That's nice of her.

4711
04:49:48,790 --> 04:49:49,370
Alright, guys.

4712
04:49:49,770 --> 04:49:50,630
I hope you enjoy your Sunday.

4713
04:49:51,410 --> 04:49:53,830
I will, uh... I'll see you next time.

4714
04:49:54,150 --> 04:49:54,790
Have a good one!

4715
04:49:54,870 --> 04:49:55,110
Bye-bye!

